    {
      "text": "Benjamin, son of Mosiah1, begins reign, Omni 1:23. drives out Lamanites, Omni 1:24 (W of M 1:13–14). given plates by Amaleki1, Omni 1:25 (W of M 1:10). hands down plates, W of M 1:11. uses sword of Laban against Lamanites, W of M 1:13. holy man, establishes peace, W of M 1:16–18 (Mosiah 1:1). sons of Benjamin named, Mosiah 1:2. teaches concerning records, Mosiah 1:3. confers kingdom on Mosiah2, Mosiah 1:10, 15 (2:30; 6:3). gives Mosiah2 records and artifacts, Mosiah 1:16. addresses people from tower, Mosiah 2:9–4:30. serves, labors with hands, Mosiah 2:12–14. urges service to fellow beings, Mosiah 2:17. teaches of Jesus’ suffering, Mosiah 3:7. teaches about Atonement, Mosiah 3:15–19. teaches about judgment, Mosiah 3:18–27. teaches people to help beggars, for all are beggars, Mosiah 4:16–19. Benjamin’s people covenant with the Lord, Mosiah 5:5. takes names of those who enter covenant, Mosiah 6:1. consecrates Mosiah2, appoints priests, Mosiah 6:3. dies, Mosiah 6:5. Benjamin’s word rehearsed by Ammon1, Mosiah 8:2–3. rising generation do not understand Benjamin’s words, Mosiah 26:1. if people could have kings like Benjamin, it would be well, Mosiah 29:13. Helaman3 asks sons to remember words of Benjamin, Hel. 5:9.",
